  "problem": "Changing pages in a centered widescreen scroll or parchment could draw new text over previous pages, making it unreadable in either language.",
  "cause": "CDocument::renderText supplied a local clip rectangle to DecoratedWindow::drawClipped, which tests screen-coordinate decoration extents. Centered vertical documents can lie wholly outside that rectangle. Their temporary background then remains transparent and matte composition retains the previous text.",
  "fix": "Pass the document screen extent as the background clip, retaining the existing screen-to-local offset and original artwork, typography, page layout and resource data.",
  "regression_before_fix": {
    "status": "failed_as_expected",
    "private_log": ".cache/scroll-redraw-regression/en/output/native.log",
    "failure": "Document redraw differs: script=131 appearance=2 wide=1 sidebar=0 language=0 page=1"
  },
